{
 "idea": {
  "id": "rev_vix",
  "family": "reversal",
  "title": "The same loser-minus-winner trade, but only on days the market is frightened",
  "why": "The reversal trade is payment for supplying liquidity, and that payment rises when dealers are stretched. Nagel (2012) found its return tracks the VIX closely. If most of the edge sits in stressed weeks, trading only then should keep the return and cut the cost of trading in quiet weeks, when the spread eats it.",
  "source": "Nagel 2012, Evaporating Liquidity",
